{
	"name": "Log completed ThunderPhone calls to Google Sheets",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Log completed ThunderPhone calls to Google Sheets\n\nWhen a ThunderPhone AI voice agent finishes a call, this workflow adds a Google Sheets row with the caller, duration, end reason and a link to the call. It does not copy transcripts or summaries.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Call completed** starts the workflow from ThunderPhone's signed webhook. It registers the webhook on publish and removes it on unpublish.\n2. **Get call details** reads the call record, and **Skip test calls** drops agent-builder test calls.\n3. **Format sheet row** picks the columns, and **Append to Google Sheet** adds the row.\n\n### Setup\n1. An instance owner or admin installs the verified **ThunderPhone** node (`n8n-nodes-thunderphone`) from the nodes panel.\n2. Add a ThunderPhone server API key (**Organization > Keys**) in n8n as a **ThunderPhone API** credential. The key's user needs the admin or owner role so the trigger can register its webhook.\n3. Create a tab named `Calls` with these headers: Call ID, Started at, Direction, From, To, Agent, Duration (s), Status, End reason, Call link.\n4. Pick the spreadsheet in **Append to Google Sheet** and publish. n8n must be reachable over public HTTPS.\n\n### Customization\n- To add the transcript or summary, add a field in **Format sheet row** from the call record's `transcripts` or `summary` and a matching column. Read the note below first.\n\n### Data handling\nCall transcripts and summaries can contain personal or health information. Add them only if your organization is allowed to store that data in the connected app, and under a BAA where health information is involved. Rows you copy into Google Sheets stay there until you delete them. Set a retention rule that fits your data.\n\nn8n keeps each execution's input, including transcripts; limit execution data retention in n8n.",
				"height": 820,
				"width": 560
			},
			"id": "e9c76817-8d4b-51cf-85a7-3860c79d988b",
			"name": "Template overview",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [-720, -200]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## 1. Receive the finished call\nThe trigger fires for phone and web calls. **Get call details** fetches the full record.",
				"height": 380,
				"width": 480,
				"color": 7
			},
			"id": "d7d73f5e-68a5-5de7-a0db-6b2b09bd61d4",
			"name": "Section: receive the call",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [-100, -20]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## 2. Write one row per call\nTest calls are skipped. Rename columns in **Format sheet row** to match your sheet headers.",
				"height": 380,
				"width": 700,
				"color": 7
			},
			"id": "1530ad29-966f-5b70-b65d-07b5c3d09315",
			"name": "Section: write the row",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [420, -20]
		},
		{
